# converge-ci-stack.service — boot-ordered reconstruct of the CI CLUSTER
# stack on the single-node k3s host. Runs converge-ci-stack.sh once per boot,
# AFTER k3s is up, AFTER the churn-slot extended resource has been reapplied
# and AFTER the GitHub App secret has been re-injected, to idempotently
# assert that resource and converge the fleet-owned local-path provisioner,
# Kueue core (waiting for its admission webhook to serve), every
# ResourceFlavor/ClusterQueue/LocalQueue, the ARC controller, all runner
# scale sets, the hook-pod-template ConfigMap, the crates proxy, the
# warm-cache CronJob, and
# the Kueue-webhook probe's re-rendered credential — from this repository,
# zero manual kubectl/helm steps. See ./converge-ci-stack.sh for the full
# sequence, why the ORDER is what it is, the scope boundary (cluster-side
# state only, not the node-local machinery), and the fail-closed
# GitHub-App-secret pre-gate.
#
# ORDERING vs. the secret: converge fail-closes if the arc-github-app-installation
# secret is absent (the script's step 2). ../../secret-reinjection/
# inject-github-app-secret.service re-creates it from the host credstore on
# every boot and orders itself Before= this unit; the After=/Wants= below
# state the same dependency from this side so it holds even if that unit's
# own ordering is ever edited. Wants (not Requires): if the secret unit fails,
# this converge still runs and fails closed with its own clear message,
# rather than being silently skipped.
#
# ORDERING vs. the churn-slot reapply (2026-09-04, item livespec-kgl3):
# reapply-node-extended-resource.service already orders itself Before= this
# unit (its header says why); the After=/Wants= below state the same
# dependency from this side, exactly as for the secret unit, and Wants= adds
# what a one-sided Before= cannot: a HAND-STARTED converge now pulls the
# reapply in too. On the 2026-09-04 06:31Z boot stale NVMe lines in
# /etc/fstab failed k3s's mount dependency and every After=k3s oneshot
# failed by dependency; an operator hand-started k3s and this converge but
# not the reapply, and the node ran with NO churn-slot capacity from 06:31Z
# to 07:52Z while the queues advertised 32. Wants (not Requires), for the
# same reason as the secret unit: if the reapply fails, this converge still
# runs, and its own step 1b asserts the capacity and re-runs the patch.
#
# oneshot (not a long-running service): it converges and exits. It is NOT
# RemainAfterExit — a converged cluster needs no held state, and leaving it
# inactive-dead after a clean exit is correct. Re-run manually any time with
# `systemctl start converge-ci-stack.service` (idempotent).
[Unit]
Description=Converge the CI cluster stack (provisioner + Kueue + queues + ARC + scale sets) on the k3s host
After=k3s.service reapply-node-extended-resource.service inject-github-app-secret.service
Requires=k3s.service
Wants=reapply-node-extended-resource.service inject-github-app-secret.service

[Service]
Type=oneshot
Environment=KUBECONFIG=/etc/rancher/k3s/k3s.yaml
ExecStart=/usr/local/lib/ci-runner-k3s/converge-ci-stack.sh

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
